completed_at: "2026-10-24T05:16:10.725Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: The public template-save option type documents supported priority input; saving numeric priority0 preserves priority0 when creating from the template; the existing string-priority and direct-create controls remain correct; invalid unsupported values receive actionable pre-write refusal; sandboxed SDK regressions prove stored values and mutation safety.
parent: pm-780f
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Export TemplatesSaveOptions from SDK aggregate/runtime and first-party package wrapper; normalize numeric, string and named priority with the shared parser before writes and reject invalid priority values."
expected_result: "Numeric priority0 survives save/show/create; invalid inputs preserve template and history bytes, and explicit create overrides still win."
actual_result: "26 linked tests pass with numeric0/4, string/named priorities, stored JSON, show/create, explicit override and byte-preserving invalid-input controls; public typecheck rejects boolean/array priority inputs. Pre-fix numeric/invalid controls fail as intended."
affected_version: 2026.10.23
